#. module: web_studio
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/web_studio/models/ir_model.py:0
msgid ""
"\n"
"                <p class=\"o_view_nocontent_smiling_face\">\n"
"                    This is your new action.\n"
"                </p>\n"
"                <p>By default, it contains a list and a form view and "
"possibly\n"
"                    other view types depending on the options you chose for "
"your model.\n"
"                </p>\n"
"                <p>\n"
"                    You can start customizing these screens by clicking on "
"the Studio icon on the\n"
"                    top right corner (you can also customize this help "
"message there).\n"
"                </p>\n"
"            "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"                <p class=\"o_view_nocontent_smiling_face\">\n"
"                    Dette er din nye handling.\n"
"                </p>\n"
"                <p>Den indeholder som standard en liste og en "
"formularvisning og muligvis\n"
"                    andre typer visninger, afhængig af de indstillinger du "
"vælger for din model.\n"
"                </p>\n"
"                <p>\n"
"                    Du kan tilpasse disse skærme ved at klikke på Studio-"
"ikonet i øverste\n"
"                    højre hjørne (der kan du også redigere denne besked.)\n"
"                </p>\n"
"            "

#. module: web_studio
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_web_studio
msgid ""
"\n"
"Studio - Customize Odoo\n"
"=======================\n"
"\n"
"This addon allows the user to customize most element of the user interface, "
"in a\n"
"simple and graphical way. It has two main features:\n"
"\n"
"* create a new application (add module, top level menu item, and default "
"action)\n"
"* customize an existing application (edit menus, actions, views, "
"translations, ...)\n"
"\n"
"Note: Only the admin user is allowed to make those customizations.\n"
msgstr ""

